  "summary": "Bind reference action inputs on an existing history and the Shop/non-Shop proof.",
  "why": "Luis approved the narrow extraction. RED 55f7a8d requires the missing producer. GREEN 4454199 exposes four repository-local constructors taking caller-owned history and explicit sources, policies, IDs, actors and clocks. Old checkpoint/context assembly is removed from fixture helpers. A fresh process prohibits test and Shop imports while initializing and proposing over three admitted non-Shop records. Missing inputs refuse; stale or malformed submission preserves exact bytes. Combined finite-action, Small Shop and fresh-import gate: 742 passed, zero skips/failures. The new 106-event sequential Shop log exactly matches its recorded predecessor SHA-256. Ruff/format/diff passed. The selected program and existing atomic owner remain authoritative. The report discloses fixture prerequisites, test-harness corrections and the remaining caller-authored lifecycle envelopes. No Robotics/Re-entry integration, new interpreter, public SDK, package change, full-repository rerun, release or push is claimed.",
